1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,500
A sound soul dwells within a sound mind and a sound body.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,500
Hey, Krona, good morning.

3
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:35,500
Oh, good morning.

4
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:37,000
Come on, let's get going.

5
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:23,000
See you in your dreams, yeah, baby.

6
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Oh, good morning.

7
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Oh, good morning.

8
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Oh, good morning.

9
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:53,320
I am forever with you so

10
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:57,260
見上がれば輝く

11
00:01:57,260 --> 00:01:59,600
月のように

12
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,280
and may be

13
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:26,000
you.

14
00:02:30,060 --> 00:02:31,280
yeah

15
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:33,200
come on corno quit hiding

16
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:41,280
there's nothing to be afraid of here

17
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:45,280
Why?

18
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:50,660
Why is everybody so nice to me?

19
00:02:51,740 --> 00:02:54,280
Why do they go out of their way to help me?

20
00:02:59,260 --> 00:02:59,820
Why?

21
00:03:01,660 --> 00:03:02,580
Good ass!

22
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:04,760
Good job, Gruner!

23
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:06,880
Take it away from him!

24
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:08,520
Come on, Gruner, you can do it!

25
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:11,260
Looks like things are starting to get better for him.

26
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:14,660
Yeah, it's slow going, but we're working on it.

27
00:03:16,580 --> 00:03:20,540
So, Sol, how have you been doing?

28
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:21,360
Huh?

29
00:03:22,260 --> 00:03:24,020
That wound you took in the chest.

30
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:31,820
Ah, it's fine.

31
00:03:32,180 --> 00:03:34,420
Anyway, dwelling too much on the past ain't cool.

32
00:03:35,060 --> 00:03:37,600
Especially when it comes to a fight we ended up losing.

33
00:03:38,060 --> 00:03:39,460
You can just forget like that?

34
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:41,400
Maka's been working hard with Krona.

35
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:45,060
I don't want to spoil that by dredging up any bad memories.

36
00:03:46,060 --> 00:03:47,040
I get it.

37
00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:49,040
All right.

38
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:50,760
Let's get in on this.

39
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:51,420
Here!

40
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:53,200
Give me that a sec.

41
00:03:53,780 --> 00:03:55,760
Your center of gravity is high, see?

42
00:03:56,460 --> 00:03:58,360
You need to bend your knees a little more.

43
00:03:58,640 --> 00:04:00,240
Relax your shoulders and then throw.

44
00:04:00,880 --> 00:04:02,020
Here, you give it a try.

45
00:04:02,020 --> 00:04:07,820
I think it's time for another party.

46
00:04:12,620 --> 00:04:13,860
Drying happiness.

47
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:15,820
Whose tears sparkle in the moonlight?

48
00:04:15,820 --> 00:04:30,120
Hey, Sol, thanks for contributing to the music selection.

49
00:04:30,580 --> 00:04:30,980
Sure.

50
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:32,880
Is this one going to be okay, though?

51
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:36,980
Well, you said to bring something catchy, so I decided on this punk record.

52
00:04:37,580 --> 00:04:39,820
But it might not work that well for this crowd.

53
00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:40,380
Yeah.

54
00:04:41,220 --> 00:04:42,900
Well then, play the piano.

55
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:44,260
There's one right there.

56
00:04:44,540 --> 00:04:45,620
Why the sudden craving?

57
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:47,780
It's been a while since I've heard you.

58
00:04:47,780 --> 00:04:49,540
I think I'll pass on that one.

59
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:51,020
I gotta take a leak.

60
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:52,300
Aw, he got away.

61
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:55,640
I had no idea he could play the piano.

62
00:04:56,820 --> 00:04:58,900
Yeah, he's only played for me once, though.

63
00:04:59,220 --> 00:05:00,860
Right before we first became partners.

64
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:02,220
What kind of song?

65
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:03,600
It's hard to explain.

66
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:05,120
Something dark and strange.

67
00:05:05,660 --> 00:05:09,340
He said, this is the kind of person I am, and just started playing.

68
00:05:11,460 --> 00:05:14,660
Something about that song and the way he played it must have gotten to me.

69
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:16,100
And we became partners.

70
00:05:16,100 --> 00:05:16,680
Hm.

71
00:05:17,780 --> 00:05:19,460
Well, I'm sorry I missed it.

72
00:05:23,140 --> 00:05:23,620
Shibatsu!

73
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:24,520
Seconds!

74
00:05:24,540 --> 00:05:25,140
Give me seconds!

75
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:26,340
Yeah, okay.

76
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:30,160
Sorry, Krona.

77
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:32,720
A noisy group like this must make you uncomfortable.

78
00:05:33,420 --> 00:05:35,600
I'm not completely used to it yet.

79
00:05:35,980 --> 00:05:38,720
But I'm not feeling uncomfortable either.

80
00:05:39,620 --> 00:05:41,320
No one's going anywhere for a bit.

81
00:05:41,740 --> 00:05:42,920
So you can take your time.

82
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:44,400
Join the group at your own pace.

83
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:45,220
Hm?

84
00:05:45,780 --> 00:05:47,740
There's no need to rush this sort of thing.

85
00:05:48,500 --> 00:05:48,820
Yo!

86
00:05:49,380 --> 00:05:51,300
What are you hanging out over here for?

87
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:52,340
It's a party.

88
00:05:52,420 --> 00:05:53,300
Let's have some fun!

89
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:58,260
What was that for?

90
00:05:58,260 --> 00:05:59,760
Don't bully Krona.

91
00:05:59,980 --> 00:06:00,760
What's up?

92
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:02,260
Someone's bullying Krona?

93
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:06,500
Krona, if someone's giving you a hard time, you just let old Blackstar know.

94
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:10,180
I'll throw him out the nearest window.

95
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:18,300
Why is everyone so nice to someone like me?

96
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:19,740
It's simple, Krona.

97
00:06:19,740 --> 00:06:19,760
It's simple, Krona.

98
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:22,260
That's just what friends do.

99
00:06:26,640 --> 00:06:28,900
If you're a friend, then feed me!

100
00:06:29,260 --> 00:06:29,620
Here!

101
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:31,040
Shibaki made it herself!

102
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:33,580
I sure hope you enjoy it.

103
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:35,620
Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

104
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:37,060
Gross.

105
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:39,040
Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

106
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:42,120
Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

107
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:57,580
Krona, come and hang out at my place next time.

108
00:06:57,580 --> 00:06:58,700
I don't mind cooking.

109
00:06:58,700 --> 00:07:02,060
It's worth it for someone with an appetite as big as Ragnarok's is.

110
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:04,860
See you later, then.

111
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:06,400
Bye-bye!

112
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:08,300
I'll see you tomorrow.

113
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:21,900
Hey, Krona!

114
00:07:22,060 --> 00:07:25,100
You should try to find a partner who can cook like that Tsubaki girl!

115
00:07:25,680 --> 00:07:26,860
How can I do that?

116
00:07:26,860 --> 00:07:28,580
I thought you were already my partner.

117
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:32,000
The party was a lot of fun, wasn't it?

118
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:34,060
The food was good, at least.

119
00:07:52,300 --> 00:07:53,840
I've been waiting for you.

120
00:07:54,220 --> 00:07:54,980
Hi, Krona.

121
00:07:54,980 --> 00:07:58,040
Lady Medusa.

122
00:07:58,040 --> 00:08:00,100
Very good, Krona.

123
00:08:00,100 --> 00:08:03,200
I wasn't sure you'd recognize me in this sad state.

124
00:08:04,320 --> 00:08:05,340
Embarrassing, isn't it?

125
00:08:05,660 --> 00:08:07,900
You've gotten all tiny, just like me!

126
00:08:08,340 --> 00:08:09,140
W-why?

127
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:11,040
Why are you back in Death City?

128
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:13,340
I came for you, Krona.

129
00:08:13,340 --> 00:08:14,340
I've been so worried about you.

130
00:08:14,340 --> 00:08:16,240
I've been so worried about you.

131
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:17,560
You're worried?

132
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:20,960
Does that mean you're here to bring me back with you?

133
00:08:20,960 --> 00:08:21,960
Oh, no.

134
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:26,480
You should stay in the academy and continue your work as my spy.

135
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:28,840
Oh, what are you talking about?

136
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:29,820
A spy?

137
00:08:29,820 --> 00:08:30,500
Me?

138
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:33,400
There's no need to be so modest about it.

139
00:08:33,560 --> 00:08:36,280
That's why you infiltrated the DWMA, right?

140
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:37,280
To become a spy?

141
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:41,840
You did a good job, but now I have a task only you can do.

142
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:44,620
There's a secret vault somewhere within the academy.

143
00:08:44,620 --> 00:08:47,240
For now, all I need you to do is find it.

144
00:08:48,340 --> 00:08:50,800
I'm counting on you, Krona.

145
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:51,560
No, wait!

146
00:08:51,660 --> 00:08:54,040
I've made some friends at the academy.

147
00:08:54,980 --> 00:08:57,340
Doing this might make them angry at me.

148
00:08:57,340 --> 00:09:00,460
But you'll do it, won't you?

149
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:02,060
For your dear mother.

150
00:09:11,740 --> 00:09:12,840
Yes, ma'am.

151
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:13,820
I understand.

152
00:09:21,300 --> 00:09:22,140
Gooby-bee!

153
00:09:22,620 --> 00:09:23,920
Things are getting interesting.

154
00:09:27,340 --> 00:09:38,420
Death City is growing thick with madness.

155
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:42,660
It won't be long before something happens.

156
00:09:57,340 --> 00:09:59,380
Folk music grows.

157
00:09:59,380 --> 00:10:00,800
You're joking, right?

158
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:01,640
Tell me you're joking.

159
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:03,420
I didn't ask for your opinion.

160
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:04,880
Seriously, though.

161
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:06,180
How can you listen to that?

162
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:07,700
Folk music is stupid.

163
00:10:08,040 --> 00:10:11,800
I may not do very well on tests, but even I know that much, dude.

164
00:10:12,180 --> 00:10:13,980
I listen to whatever I want.

165
00:10:14,060 --> 00:10:14,800
Leave me alone.

166
00:10:17,100 --> 00:10:17,660
Krona?

167
00:10:18,100 --> 00:10:19,920
Oh, sorry.

168
00:10:20,400 --> 00:10:22,580
I think I'll head back to my room now.

169
00:10:23,380 --> 00:10:24,260
See you tomorrow.

170
00:10:24,460 --> 00:10:25,040
We'll see ya.

171
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:29,800
What's wrong with him?

172
00:10:30,360 --> 00:10:32,500
He's been more withdrawn than usual lately.

173
00:10:33,100 --> 00:10:33,440
Really?

174
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:35,440
How can you tell the difference?

175
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:45,580
You'd better get moving, or Medusa won't be happy.

176
00:10:45,580 --> 00:10:56,400
Good to see you, Justin.

177
00:10:56,680 --> 00:10:57,440
How are things?

178
00:11:00,740 --> 00:11:02,360
Hey, Spirit, give me a hand.

179
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:04,500
Justin's got his headphones in as usual,

180
00:11:04,680 --> 00:11:06,740
and he can't read my lips with this mask on.

181
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:08,980
Do me a favor and repeat everything I say

182
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:10,260
for the rest of the conversation.

183
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:10,840
Cool.

184
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:13,560
What, am I some kind of parrot now?

185
00:11:13,980 --> 00:11:15,800
Can't he just take out the headphones?

186
00:11:16,220 --> 00:11:18,020
Okay, now repeat after me.

187
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:21,120
Justin, I called you into the death room today

188
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:23,880
because I need to explain the new assignment I'm giving you.

189
00:11:24,420 --> 00:11:25,700
Hey, hold on.

190
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:29,660
These are your orders from Lord Death.

191
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:30,500
Listen up.

192
00:11:30,760 --> 00:11:32,620
The reason you were called in here today

193
00:11:32,620 --> 00:11:34,560
is to receive your latest assignment.

194
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:35,520
Okay?

195
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:36,480
What is it?

196
00:11:36,980 --> 00:11:38,920
This is a very important mission.

197
00:11:39,540 --> 00:11:41,360
This is a very important mission.

198
00:11:41,980 --> 00:11:45,140
You're aware that because of her extraordinary scouting abilities,

199
00:11:45,420 --> 00:11:48,000
Azusa has been given the task of hunting down the Kishin?

200
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:51,380
You know Azusa's the one in charge of hunting down the Kishin, right?

201
00:11:51,760 --> 00:11:53,840
But there's a limit to what she can do from here.

202
00:11:54,100 --> 00:11:55,500
That's why I need you to help.

203
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:57,160
While she's using her eyes,

204
00:11:57,240 --> 00:11:58,680
I want you to use your legs.

205
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:00,900
Travel everywhere searching for the Kishin.

206
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:03,380
But she can only do so much with her eyes.

207
00:12:03,580 --> 00:12:04,580
That's where you come in.

208
00:12:04,840 --> 00:12:06,020
You're gonna be her legs.

209
00:12:06,260 --> 00:12:07,880
Hey, that's not what I said.

210
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:09,700
Repeat it properly from now on.

211
00:12:10,020 --> 00:12:12,020
You're taking too long to explain it.

212
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:13,300
Say that again.

213
00:12:14,660 --> 00:12:15,500
Yeah, fine.

214
00:12:15,540 --> 00:12:16,180
I got it.

215
00:12:17,680 --> 00:12:18,440
Now then.

216
00:12:18,960 --> 00:12:20,520
Here's what I'm hoping will happen.

217
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:22,980
If you can make enough noise during your search,

218
00:12:23,180 --> 00:12:25,420
you may be able to flush out the Cowardly Kishin

219
00:12:25,420 --> 00:12:26,520
from wherever it's hiding.

220
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:28,300
Do you understand the assignment?

221
00:12:28,780 --> 00:12:30,340
Here's what I'm hoping will happen.

222
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:32,720
If you can make enough noise during your search,

223
00:12:32,900 --> 00:12:35,200
you may be able to flush out the Cowardly Kishin

224
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:36,320
from wherever it's hiding.

225
00:12:36,720 --> 00:12:38,200
Do you understand the assignment?

226
00:12:38,560 --> 00:12:40,780
Oh, what a truly wondrous assignment!

227
00:12:41,160 --> 00:12:43,120
I accept the mission with great pleasure.

228
00:12:43,580 --> 00:12:45,140
I'm counting on you to succeed.

229
00:12:45,440 --> 00:12:47,040
I'm counting on you to succeed.

230
00:12:47,460 --> 00:12:47,840
Right.

231
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:53,140
Looks like the hallway's off-limits from here.

232
00:12:53,940 --> 00:12:54,660
Go beep-beep!

233
00:12:55,420 --> 00:12:57,800
Which might mean it's a good place to look for the vault.

234
00:12:58,640 --> 00:13:01,260
What if somebody sees me wandering down here?

235
00:13:01,580 --> 00:13:03,280
What am I supposed to do then?

236
00:13:03,360 --> 00:13:05,620
It's not my problem if you get yourself caught.

237
00:13:05,620 --> 00:13:07,620
Hello?

238
00:13:07,940 --> 00:13:08,680
Who's there?

239
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,380
Oh, it's you, Krona.

240
00:13:12,940 --> 00:13:13,960
What are you doing?

241
00:13:14,040 --> 00:13:15,440
You shouldn't be down here, you know.

242
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:17,520
This area's off-limits.

243
00:13:17,940 --> 00:13:19,820
Um, I, uh...

244
00:13:19,820 --> 00:13:20,580
Well, I...

245
00:13:20,580 --> 00:13:21,840
You saved us, Marie!

246
00:13:22,180 --> 00:13:23,700
We were trying to find our room,

247
00:13:23,760 --> 00:13:25,100
and we lost our way!

248
00:13:25,540 --> 00:13:27,840
Well, I'm actually a little lost myself.

249
00:13:28,320 --> 00:13:30,040
The Academy's layout is confusing.

250
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:31,680
I still don't understand it.

251
00:13:31,680 --> 00:13:33,880
But we'll figure it out somehow.

252
00:13:34,020 --> 00:13:34,900
Just leave it to me.

253
00:13:35,100 --> 00:13:35,700
Don't worry.

254
00:13:35,800 --> 00:13:37,000
I'll help you find your room.

255
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:40,640
Now, let's see here.

256
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:42,520
It's this way!

257
00:13:42,840 --> 00:13:44,000
You sure about that?

258
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:51,300
Well, we made it.

259
00:13:51,920 --> 00:13:52,580
Thanks a lot.

260
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:54,340
We couldn't have done it without you.

261
00:13:55,260 --> 00:13:56,820
If you run into any more difficulties,

262
00:13:57,020 --> 00:13:58,800
don't hesitate to let me know, okay?

263
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:00,620
I'll be glad to help.

264
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,060
Except with directions.

265
00:14:04,460 --> 00:14:05,780
I'll leave you here then.

266
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:06,280
Good night!

267
00:14:06,640 --> 00:14:08,520
The teacher's office is that way.

268
00:14:08,520 --> 00:14:27,920
Ribbit.

269
00:14:28,920 --> 00:14:30,260
I hate this.

270
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:32,600
I can't stand going back and forth

271
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:34,420
from such a dangerous place.

272
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:35,680
Erica...

273
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:36,620
What's your progress?

274
00:14:37,220 --> 00:14:38,860
Do you know where the secret vault is?

275
00:14:39,260 --> 00:14:40,860
I can't do this.

276
00:14:41,540 --> 00:14:43,660
I can't deal with this kind of situation.

277
